  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "S1",
      "priority": "P1",
      "title": "Structured repair bypasses replay-state origin bookkeeping",
      "file": "src/core/Agent.ts",
      "start": 3388,
      "end": 3390,
      "status": "open",
      "reproduction": "Nonrouted JSON run: portable malformed response, then repaired JSON with persistent signed thinking. Checkpoint retains the signature but no providerStateBinding; a subsequent request hook switches model and successfully dispatches the signature to wrong-owner. Ordinary opaque output and routed repair controls block the switch. A provider_state variant also lacks the origin; top-level reasoning returned by repair is dropped from history.",
      "fix": "Use one protocol-aware replacement/commit boundary for all structured repair/reformat responses, preserving ordered replay items and the actual admitted origin, retain legacy portable hook behavior and optional snapshot compatibility."
    },
    {
      "id": "S2",
      "priority": "P1",
      "title": "Budget-rejected resumption loses its original route, format and ModelTask",
      "file": "src/core/Agent.ts",
      "start": 1794,
      "end": 1798,
      "status": "open",
      "reproduction": "Suspend on fast with a shared maxCalls:2 task, spending both calls. First ordinary event resume rejects maxCalls without another provider call. Repeat the same event without options: selector runs again, a new task admits main, and inherited output_parsed is absent. The original task remains at two calls; the wait ran only once. A rejected explicit route override control preserves the original origin.",
      "fix": "Retain or atomically restore suspended ownership/effective options when resume fails before actual dispatch/admission, rather than clearing at setup. Do not obtain another allowance by retrying the same event. Reuse explicit host cancellation/abandonment semantics for intentional new work and preserve action receipts."
    },
    {
      "id": "S3",
      "priority": "P2",
      "title": "Suspension is checkpointed and published before structured finalization",
      "file": "src/core/Agent.ts",
      "start": 2418,
      "end": 2428,
      "status": "open",
      "reproduction": "With ordinary context (no selective assembly), a malformed suspension wrap-up is saved before outer repair. run() returns suspended with parsed FORMATTED and live history matches, but saved history still contains NOT_JSON and lacks FORMATTED. With maxCalls:2, repair cannot dispatch, yet the raw checkpoint/correlation and one execution:suspended event already exist before run() throws. A Google-style tool/format composition control with an already valid JSON wrap-up also publishes its suspension before a mandatory formatting call fails the two-call cap; malformed output is not required.",
      "fix": "Finalize the settled suspension candidate on every context path before committing/publishing a successful formatted suspension, while durably retaining the acknowledged wait and preserving recoverable route/task authority on formatting, cancellation, budget or storage failure. Never repeat the external registration to recover."
    }
  ],
